{"id":183676706861922,"type":"album","name":"Tubthumper","artist":"Chumbawamba","year":1997,"weight":16,"info":{"cover":"https://dn710807.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-e2da61ad-6406-349f-b096-e354858c0d00/mbid-e2da61ad-6406-349f-b096-e354858c0d00-23161775745.jpg","kind":"Album","tracks":12,"scaruffi":7.0,"yt":"b5BHSNRpZcc","links":{"spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/album/5yaumQgV6xGqCy014aOREt","youtube":"https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=OLAK5uy_k4T9jygJnRGCR-7ObiYgVY0QBJGqiXVTk","rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/chumbawamba/tubthumper"},"desc":"Chumbawamba had been kicking around the British anarchist and indie scene for years, having released seven studio albums, before \"Tubthumper\" unexpectedly brought the band to the top of the charts around the world through the album's title track \"Tubthumping\". The band now being mostly remembered as a one hit wonder, the song is a giddily celebratory blend of big dance beats, pop hooks, and football chants. The sudden success of the group is commonly attributed to an abrupt change in style from their early roots in punk music. However, \"Tubthumper\" sees the band continue their musical direction as laid out ."},"artist_ref":{"id":216677698095833,"name":"Chumbawamba","info":{"img":"https://cdn-images.dzcdn.net/images/artist/69ce49266046267d4e2c600abcddbec0/1000x1000-000000-80-0-0.jpg"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":210192360016800,"type":"genre","name":"Alternative Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":2664,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":31482837869539,"type":"genre","name":"Punk","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":2333,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":18872195504512,"type":"genre","name":"Pop Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":740,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":223122507869858,"type":"genre","name":"Dance-Pop","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":311,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":186049650705997,"type":"genre","name":"Alternative Dance","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":28